This code defines two regular expression patterns to match claims and premises. The `findall` method returns all non-overlapping matches of these patterns in the input string. Then it iterates over the matches and tags them accordingly. Finally, it prints out the modified sentence with the claimed spans surrounded by `<claim>` and `</claim>` or `<premise>` and `</premise>`. 

